              "short": "$9,\\ 11,\\ 13,\\ 15$",
              "worked": "Let $2n+1$ be the first odd number, where $n$ is an integer.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2n+1)+(2n+3)+(2n+5)+(2n+7)&=48\\\\8n+16&=48\\\\8n&=32\\\\n&=4\\end{align*}$$\nThe numbers are $2(4)+1,\\ 2(4)+3,\\ 2(4)+5,\\ 2(4)+7$, so they are $9,\\ 11,\\ 13,\\ 15$.\nCheck: $9+11+13+15=48$.",
